# Git
# .git/ is DELIBERATELY NOT excluded. Nerdbank.GitVersioning derives the package version from
# commit history, and Containers/AppHost/Dockerfile does COPY . ., so without it every in-image
# build trips the guard in ServiceVersioning.props. NBGV does not fail on a missing repository on
# its own - it quietly produces a height-0 prerelease that sorts BELOW the real version. Costs
# roughly 5 MB of build context, against a DockerPackages folder several times larger, and .git
# reaches only the build stage: the final image copies /app/publish alone.
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Visual Studio / VS Code
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosspath
*.sln.docstates

# Build results
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/out/
**/.vs/

# NuGet
*.nupkg
*.snupkg
.nuget/
packages/

# Test results
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
[Bb]uild[Ll]og.*
*.trx
*.coverage
*.coveragexml

# Documentation and analysis files
*.md
**/*.md

# Text files (but allow LICENSE.txt)
*.txt
!LICENSE.txt
!**/LICENSE.txt

# Release artifacts
Release/
MakeRelease/

# IDE and editor files
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store

# Local development
LocalWebService/

# Node modules (if any)
**/node_modules/

# Logs
*.log
